  "name": "Support Vector Regression",
  "description": "Support Vector Regression with an RBF kernel on standardised inputs and target. Slow on the market panel.",
  "preprocessing": "`TransformedTargetRegressor` around `Pipeline`: ColumnTransformer (numeric features \u2192 median imputation fitted on the training rows, with a binary missing-indicator column per feature, then StandardScaler; categorical features (the market identifier) \u2192 one-hot encoding, unknown categories ignored) \u2192 `SVR(kernel='rbf', C, epsilon, gamma)`. The target is standardised (log1p first when `log_target` is on) and predictions are transformed back to guests. Kernel cost grows quadratically with rows: the 29k-row market panel takes several minutes. With the `floor_zero` policy the pipeline is wrapped in `NonNegative`, which floors predictions at 0 (raw negatives are still counted in the metadata).",
